    <node id="&quot;双生数组&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The event of defining and creating a 'twin array' which requires an array of even size with exactly two types of elements that appear the same number of times. The entire problem revolves around this concept."&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组 (twin array) is defined as an array with even size, exactly 2 distinct elements, and equal counts of these elements. It represents a specific state or event that needs to be achieved through operations."&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组 is a special type of array where the size is even, there are exactly two distinct elements, and those two elements appear an equal number of times."&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组 is the event or condition that occurs when an array is transformed to meet specific criteria: even size, exactly two element types, and each appearing the same number of times, as defined by小红."&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组 is a concept defined by 小红 as an array of even size with exactly two distinct elements both appearing the same number of times."&lt;SEP&gt;"双生数组 is a defined concept where an array needs to have an even size, exactly two distinct elements, and both elements occurring the same number of times."</data>
